1
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:41,117
See you

2
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:48,200
next

3
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:49,670
time.

4
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,220
What's going on?

5
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:56,277
How did you get here in the first place?

6
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:58,007
This is dangerous, you know.

7
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,297
What are you...

8
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:02,417
Pleased to meet you.

9
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,912
I'm Sniper King, the King of the Snipers.

10
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:08,720
To make a long story short,
I've come to rescue you.

11
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:10,214
You're really serious.

12
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,897
I'm not alone, of course.

13
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:14,357
Your friend Sanji and a
cyborg thug named Franky

14
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:16,697
are currently engaged
in battle on this train.

15
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:20,133
They kept the enemy busy long
enough for me to come here.

16
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:21,510
Furthermore,

17
00:02:21,593 --> 00:02:22,797
Captain Luffy and the
rest of the Straw Hats

18
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,077
are following closely on another C-train.

19
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:27,780
I hear he's bringing
a small army with him.

20
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:36,380
On my way here, I peeked inside
the other train cars. Frankly,

21
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:40,777
I believe the four agents in the car
behind us may prove too great a challenge.

22
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:45,272
If possible, I would like to escape
with you before Sanji has to face them.

23
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:52,870
Come.

24
00:02:52,953 --> 00:02:54,620
Let's run away. Together.

25
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:03,359
What's the matter?

26
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:04,817
There's no need to worry.

27
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,488
I've made all of the
necessary preparations.

28
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,150
Here.

29
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:10,766
These octo-shoes are for you.

30
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:12,817
If you use them on your hands and feet,

31
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:15,897
you can climb through the window and
stick to the outer panels of the C-train.

32
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:18,340
Quickly, put them on before they notice.

33
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:20,440
I won't go. Why not?

34
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,780
I don't know why you're doing this.

35
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:27,777
I told you very clearly that
I wouldn't see you again.

36
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:30,860
I said that I would never
return to the Straw Hats.

37
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,120
The situation has changed.

38
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:40,577
They know why you turned yourself in.

39
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:44,140
That ice gentleman from the
shipyard clarified everything.

40
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:48,000
So he survived after all?

41
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:51,660
But still, that doesn't change my mind.

42
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,540
I won't go with you no matter what.

43
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,311
Enough with that already.

44
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:57,960
Don't you get it?

45
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:01,591
They aren't so weak that they
need you to worry about them.

46
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,173
What were you thinking?

47
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:07,560
Accepting such a stupid deal before
talking to the rest of the crew?

48
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:10,259
You think they'd be happy to go on?

49
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:13,297
Knowing that one of their friends
had thrown her life away for them?

50
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:15,460
Now that they know why you left,

51
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:18,237
they'll follow you to the
depths of hell if they have to.

52
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:21,555
And they'll bust every skull
they can on the way there.

53
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:23,451
You don't get it, do you?

54
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:26,000
That's the kind of guy Luffy is.

55
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:29,391
How many times do I have to tell you this?

56
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:32,737
Even if you think you can save
me, I don't want your help.

57
00:04:32,820 --> 00:04:34,520
Don't you care how I feel?

58
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,020
Come on, give me a break.

59
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,682
Hey, keep it down in there, you.

60
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,360
What's the matter?

61
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:48,308
Now that we're getting
close to Eni's lobby,

62
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:52,208
is that cool exterior of yours
finally starting to melt away?

63
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,660
Well, you can cry all you like,

64
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:59,212
but there's no point in lamenting your
fate after it's already been sealed.

65
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:00,480
Really, I'm fine.

66
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:03,910
Strange.

67
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,673
That's not the reaction I was expecting.

68
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:11,700
I can't put my finger on it, but
there's something different about her.

69
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:15,204
Maybe it's just my imagination.

70
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,720
I said I'm fine.

71
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,720
Now, please, just leave me alone.

72
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:24,620
This is definitely fishy.

73
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:27,709
Why is she goofing off
at a time like this?

74
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:33,450
Ravideers?

75
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:41,607
I'd like to welcome you to the
wonderful world of ramen Kenpo!

76
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:44,880
That is the lamest power-up ever.

77
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:46,080
Go, go, go!

78
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:47,740
Here I come!

79
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:50,340
Ramen Gin Po!

80
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:52,840
Pork punch fake attack!

81
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:03,615
That's the same useless punch
from before, only bigger.

82
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,220
Ah, damn it!

83
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:15,144
I'm stuck in this stupid thing!

84
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,640
Go, go, go, go!

85
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,040
Go, go, go, go, go!

86
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:34,377
So what do you think?

87
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:37,872
My ramen Cape attacks are
pretty impressive, aren't they?

88
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:40,377
It's kind of hard to look cool when your

89
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:43,048
arm and leg are buried
in noodles like that.

90
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:48,182
And now I believe it's time to pay you back
for all those kits you gave me earlier.

91
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:59,100
What the hell are you
getting dizzy for, you idiot?

92
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:04,777
You were trying to make me woozy using
your freaky eyebrows again, weren't you?

93
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:05,690
Bad move!

94
00:07:05,773 --> 00:07:07,800
You're gonna pay for that!

95
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:14,720
Ah, dammit!

96
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:17,780
It's impossible to fight back like this!

97
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,480
Here comes my noodle soul press!

98
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:34,380
Once a more! Kiss!

99
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,240
Another helping!

100
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,680
Another helping!

101
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,060
Another helping!

102
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:42,057
Another helping! Another

103
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:49,140
helping!

104
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:53,516
Finally, I'm afraid.

105
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,760
Go, go, go!

106
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:00,955
That's what you get for
underestimating me, you Moon!

107
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:05,200
No one stands a chance against
my madman, Ramen Kenpo!

108
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:09,837
If I attack him, I'm going to get
caught in those noodles again.

109
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:12,744
I'll just have to avoid
that stupid suit of his.

110
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:15,340
Go, go, go!

111
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:16,840
Have a taste of this!

112
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:19,820
Ramen and Kyoza combo!

113
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:21,870
Clappy!

114
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:31,114
And that leaves me only one place
where I can attack this annoying clown.

115
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:36,070
Escalo!

116
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:38,000
Run at me!

117
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:54,872
As you can see, I don't have a weak spot.

118
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:58,237
And I've already figured
out your fighting style.

119
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:00,917
Every one of your attacks
is some form of kicking.

120
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,647
So if I lock down your
legs, you're finished.

121
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:06,077
Go, go, go, go!

122
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:07,980
Sucks to be you, huh?

123
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:12,280
No matter what you do, you'll still
end up getting stuck in my soup.

124
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:15,650
Now, Mr.

125
00:09:15,733 --> 00:09:18,737
Wet Noodle, while we're at
it, try this one on for size!

126
00:09:18,820 --> 00:09:19,860
Ramen Kenpo!

127
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,394
Multi-noodles, please!

128
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:34,980
What the heck did you do to my noodles?!

129
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:44,100
I turned that hunk of pasta
fettolini into a platter.

130
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:46,310
Huh?

131
00:09:46,393 --> 00:09:47,340
Some sort of trick?

132
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:49,670
Hey!

133
00:09:49,753 --> 00:09:52,405
You sloshed my noodle
fist to shreds, you jerk!

134
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:59,040
A chef must fight without using his
hands or knives. Those are sacred.

135
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:02,574
So it's always been my policy
to not use them in battle.

136
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,566
But since we're in a kitchen,

137
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:11,100
And you're using food as a weapon that
changes things a bit now, doesn't it?

138
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:16,297
Well, I knew you were a pain in the
butt, but that one really takes the cake.

139
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:17,380
Thousand noodles!

140
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:28,480
Trying to look cool, you
instant little punk, huh?

141
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:31,917
An amateur cook like you shouldn't
even touch my precious kitchen knives,

142
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:32,830
you hear me?

143
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:35,860
Those are meant for
trained professionals only!

144
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:40,580
Say I sincerely apologize for
my insolence in your kitchen,

145
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:44,154
but I'm going to let you in
on a little culinary secret?

146
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:47,820
It's time for a demonstration!

147
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:56,120
This is how a real chef gracefully
handles his kitchen knives.

148
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:08,480
I'm hammered!

149
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:09,940
Paper art.

150
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:29,320
How about a taste of fresh fire?

151
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:34,060
Has this guy lost his mind?

152
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:35,888
He jumped out over the sea!

153
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:36,990
Moonwalk!

154
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:44,888
How in the hell did this freak
jump back in midair like that?

155
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:48,920
Why doesn't my tempest kick
have any effect on him?

156
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:51,652
There's something strange about his body.

157
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:55,020
I've had enough of you! Likewise!

158
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,320
What the hell are you?

159
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:09,960
Are we there yet?

160
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:11,316
Where's Bashin' Tom?

161
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,500
It's Puffin' Tom.

162
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:14,977
Anyway, get inside
before you catch a cold.

163
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:17,857
You just changed clothes and
you're soaking wet already.

164
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:18,900
I don't care.

165
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:21,560
It's more awesome up here. Fine.

166
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:24,660
Now, Gum-Gum!

167
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:27,740
300-caliber cannon!

168
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:29,290
Boom!

169
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:30,330
Whoa!

170
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:35,180
Would all of you stop screwing around?

171
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:37,900
We're bored.

172
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,177
Polish your weapons or something.

173
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,554
What's wrong with you?

174
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:43,760
Uh, yeah.

175
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:49,324
I tried to tell those guys the same thing
earlier, but they wouldn't listen to me.

176
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:52,440
Hey, check it out!

177
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:55,560
There's a train in front of us!

178
00:12:58,300 --> 00:12:59,940
It's the Puffing Tom!

179
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,979
Seems a bit early, don't you think?

180
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:08,530
Damn it.

181
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:10,317
What's going to happen to us now?

182
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:12,117
There's no engine on this car.

183
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,906
All we can do is wait it out.

184
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:15,900
Ah! Another way!

185
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:18,759
Oh, this storm is still pretty bad.

186
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,477
You think someone will come save us?

187
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:21,390
Hey, guys!

188
00:13:21,473 --> 00:13:23,137
There's something approaching from behind.

189
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:24,050
Really?

190
00:13:24,133 --> 00:13:25,351
It must be a rescue ship.

191
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:26,940
I don't think so.

192
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,917
Actually, it looks like
it's coming on the railway.

193
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:30,920
There's no way.

194
00:13:31,420 --> 00:13:34,577
There's only one Sea Train in the
world, and we're on it right now.

195
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,300
Besides, it's Aqua Laguna.

196
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:38,737
No one could make it out
of Water 7 in this weather.

197
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:41,760
Well, if it's not a train, then...

198
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:47,000
What the heck is it?

199
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,077
That's the buffing tom, all right.

200
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,572
But it's just a caboose.

201
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:52,760
There's no engine.

202
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:55,217
And it doesn't look like it's moving.

203
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:56,297
That can't be right.

204
00:13:56,380 --> 00:13:57,620
What's going on here?

205
00:13:58,140 --> 00:14:00,434
Does this mean it got detached somehow?

206
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:01,450
Huh!

207
00:14:01,533 --> 00:14:04,137
Maybe something happened and
Sandy and Usopp were on there.

208
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:05,940
Big bro Franky, too!

209
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:09,917
Well, I hope not, because
we're about to crash into him!

210
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,294
Granny, hit the brake!

211
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:13,700
I already told you now, didn't I?

212
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:14,820
We don't got one.

213
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:17,420
We're gonna crash!

214
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,780
Luffy, what are you gonna do?

215
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:24,500
I'm flying over to see what's up.

216
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:25,660
Now, come, go!

217
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,330
Rockets!

218
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:29,210
Whoa!

219
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:32,246
There's something in the sky!

220
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,020
What happened?

221
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:49,940
Ow, ow, ow!

222
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:52,380
All right, I made it!

223
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:56,980
Who the hell is this weirdo? Hello? Saji?

224
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:58,281
Are you in here?

225
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,540
Poor Usopp.

226
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:04,677
Hey, Saji!

227
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:05,920
You hear me?

228
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,200
It's maybe over there.

229
00:15:14,060 --> 00:15:15,380
Wait a sec.

230
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:16,860
I know that face.

231
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,140
It's Straw Hat Luffy!

232
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:26,700
Hello!

233
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:31,060
Are you there, Saji?

234
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:34,630
I can't hear you!

235
00:15:34,713 --> 00:15:35,543
Shut up!

236
00:15:35,626 --> 00:15:36,520
I can't hear you!

237
00:15:39,460 --> 00:15:40,500
Bring it on!

238
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:42,092
We're not scared of you!

239
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:43,940
Where's Sanji? Wait, what?

240
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:47,420
I don't know who that is!
Sanji! He's my friend!

241
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,600
Sorry, never heard of him!

242
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,200
Too bad. See ya!

243
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:56,680
Shoot him!

244
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,713
Strawhead's coming out!

245
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:08,057
Looks like they're shooting
him, and he's saying no!

246
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:11,905
Well, whatever happened, the train
cars must be full of marines.

247
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:14,180
Well, what's the plan, boatman?

248
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:18,559
If we don't move those cars out of
the way, we might get knocked off!

249
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:27,240
Holy crap, it is a Sea Train after all.

250
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:28,857
They're going to ram right into us.

251
00:16:28,940 --> 00:16:33,469
Yeah, and if they don't slow down soon,
we're going to get smashed to pieces.

252
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,959
Let the Franky family handle this.

253
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:38,277
We'll dismantle them
before they can hit us.

254
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:39,340
What may help?

255
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:40,989
I want to break stuff too.

256
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,122
Hear that, men?

257
00:16:42,380 --> 00:16:44,260
Get to work. Yeah!

258
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:46,390
Hey!

259
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:47,990
Roronoa!

260
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,920
Hear that, Roronoa?

261
00:16:50,060 --> 00:16:51,295
He's calling for you.

262
00:16:52,180 --> 00:16:53,700
Go ahead! Cut him!

263
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:57,070
